1
00:02:01,250 --> 00:02:02,790
Sanji-chan!

2
00:02:02,790 --> 00:02:04,210
I'm on my way!

3
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:08,550
I'll...

4
00:02:10,760 --> 00:02:11,550
...live...

5
00:02:13,010 --> 00:02:15,760
...here!

6
00:02:15,760 --> 00:02:18,930
Sanji-chan, you're so funny!

7
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:24,270
He seems to have recovered after all.
By his willpower alone?

8
00:02:24,270 --> 00:02:26,320
I wanna swim like you guys.

9
00:02:26,320 --> 00:02:29,110
Luffy-chin, you can swim with a bubble on.

10
00:02:29,110 --> 00:02:29,860
Really?

11
00:02:29,860 --> 00:02:33,530
Yeah, any craftsman in the city
can make one for you right away.

12
00:02:33,530 --> 00:02:36,890
I'm glad because if he has a nosebleed now,

13
00:02:36,890 --> 00:02:38,750
we don't have blood for a transfusion.

14
00:02:38,740 --> 00:02:41,620
And Sanji's blood type is very rare.

15
00:02:41,600 --> 00:02:43,110
Hey, Camie.

16
00:02:41,620 --> 00:02:44,330
Huh? That's not good, is it?

17
00:02:44,570 --> 00:02:48,400
There is somebody that I really
wanna see on the Fish-Man Island.

18
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:51,450
Who is it? The Mermaid Princess?

19
00:02:51,450 --> 00:02:51,950
Nope.

20
00:02:53,490 --> 00:02:54,780
It's Jimbei!

21
00:02:56,870 --> 00:02:58,790
Boss Jimbei?

22
00:02:58,790 --> 00:03:02,620
Hey Luffy, you mean Jimbei the Warlord?!

23
00:03:02,620 --> 00:03:06,340
No, he resigned during the war so he's the former Warlord.

24
00:03:06,340 --> 00:03:08,550
Yeah, he's my friend!

25
00:03:08,550 --> 00:03:13,930
What's up with you?
You know the pirate empress, too.

26
00:03:13,930 --> 00:03:19,430
When Ace died 2 years ago, I didn't lose heart...

27
00:03:19,430 --> 00:03:21,690
...thanks to him!

28
00:03:21,490 --> 00:03:24,080
I wanna see Jimbei!

29
00:03:24,080 --> 00:03:26,580
See you at the Fish-Man Island in 2 years!

30
00:03:26,580 --> 00:03:31,090
I'm looking forward to the day
when you and your friends visit us!

31
00:03:32,340 --> 00:03:35,270
We made a promise to meet
again on this island.

32
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:40,890
Oh yeah, I read in the newspaper
that you were with Jimbei.

33
00:03:40,890 --> 00:03:42,560
Yoo-hoo!

34
00:03:46,940 --> 00:03:48,440
Where's Jimbei?

35
00:03:48,440 --> 00:03:52,980
Um, Boss is not on the island now.

36
00:03:52,980 --> 00:03:53,900
Huh?

37
00:03:53,900 --> 00:03:58,160
He resigned from the Warlords
during the war 2 years ago.

38
00:03:58,160 --> 00:04:02,700
So the former members of the Fish-Man
Pirates could no longer stay here

39
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:06,120
and they left with Boss Jimbei.

40
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:09,500
What?! So I can't see him here?

41
00:04:09,960 --> 00:04:16,010
It's a long story. But the war had a
lot of effects on this island too...

42
00:04:16,010 --> 00:04:19,010
--Camie!
--Camie!

43
00:04:19,010 --> 00:04:19,680
Camie!

44
00:04:21,140 --> 00:04:23,100
--A ship is coming!
--It might be!

45
00:04:23,100 --> 00:04:25,810
--The royal family's ship!
--Maybe no one's on it!

46
00:04:25,810 --> 00:04:27,350
I'm sure somebody is!

47
00:04:27,850 --> 00:04:30,230
Who's on it, Medaka-chin sisters?

48
00:04:30,230 --> 00:04:31,230
We don't know yet.

49
00:04:31,230 --> 00:04:35,320
--You don't often see the royal family's ship.
--They seldom come here.

50
00:04:35,320 --> 00:04:39,320
Maybe they're coming to catch Luffy-chin
and the others for illegal entry!

51
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:40,160
So what?

52
00:04:40,160 --> 00:04:41,120
What?

53
00:04:41,120 --> 00:04:43,280
You guys need to hide!

54
00:04:44,450 --> 00:04:46,250
Sanji-chan, this way!

55
00:04:46,250 --> 00:04:47,250
Okay!

56
00:04:51,080 --> 00:04:54,500
RYUGU PALACE

57
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:56,670
Is it the royal family's gondola?

58
00:04:56,670 --> 00:04:57,720
You think so?

59
00:04:57,720 --> 00:04:58,800
--It is!
--Maybe!

60
00:04:58,800 --> 00:05:00,090
--I bet so!
--So what?

61
00:05:00,090 --> 00:05:04,050
But it can't be somebody
from the royal family!

62
00:05:04,050 --> 00:05:07,180
They don't bother coming all the
way to this corner of the island.

63
00:05:17,940 --> 00:05:23,370
The Neptune 3 brothers-sama are here!

64
00:05:25,870 --> 00:05:28,750
Hello, girls of the cove.

65
00:05:26,540 --> 00:05:31,290
RYUGU KINGDOM THE NEPTUNE 3 BROTHERS

66
00:05:28,750 --> 00:05:31,290
I want to ask something.

67
00:05:31,870 --> 00:05:34,250
--Princes!
--What brought you here?

68
00:05:34,670 --> 00:05:36,380
Princes?

69
00:05:37,880 --> 00:05:39,800
No, Sanji-chan!

70
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:44,920
Hide here and stay still.

71
00:05:45,620 --> 00:05:47,150
Hey, what is...

72
00:05:52,300 --> 00:05:56,220
I received a report of an illegal entry.

73
00:05:53,800 --> 00:05:58,010
FIRST SON - FUKABOSHI (SHARK MERMAN)

74
00:05:56,220 --> 00:05:57,890
Didn't they come here?

75
00:05:58,260 --> 00:06:00,970
If you've seen them, tell me-fa-so-la-ti-do!

76
00:05:58,470 --> 00:06:03,770
SECOND SON - RYUBOSHI (OARFISH MERMAN)

77
00:06:00,970 --> 00:06:04,100
If you haven't seen them, that's fine-mi-re-do!

78
00:06:04,100 --> 00:06:07,100
Moonfish! Shake, shake!

79
00:06:05,730 --> 00:06:09,810
THIRD SON - MANBOSHI (MOONFISH MERMAN)

80
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:09,810
I wanna stay here and play!

81
00:06:09,810 --> 00:06:12,230
We haven't seen anybody.

82
00:06:12,230 --> 00:06:15,280
Are they that important?

83
00:06:15,280 --> 00:06:19,160
That you princes have
to come all the way here?

84
00:06:19,620 --> 00:06:24,040
Well, I'm not sure if they're
who I think they are yet.

85
00:06:24,040 --> 00:06:26,500
He's not sure-mi-re-do!

86
00:06:27,080 --> 00:06:29,170
I can't hold it any longer!

87
00:06:29,170 --> 00:06:32,380
Everybody, let's dance together!

88
00:06:37,760 --> 00:06:39,390
What's going on?

89
00:06:40,640 --> 00:06:43,890
Hey, look! They're the
princes of Neptune's army!

90
00:06:43,890 --> 00:06:45,310
Why're they here?

91
00:06:45,810 --> 00:06:48,440
What a pain in the ass. What should we do?

92
00:06:48,890 --> 00:06:50,760
Let's see how things go.

93
00:06:53,140 --> 00:06:55,940
Hmmm. Okay. Thank you very much.

94
00:06:56,390 --> 00:06:58,350
We'll check somewhere else.

95
00:06:58,350 --> 00:07:01,110
Sorry to bother you when you're having fun.

96
00:07:01,110 --> 00:07:03,940
Let's dance another time!

97
00:07:03,940 --> 00:07:06,450
Sorry for the bother-so-fa-mi-re-do!

98
00:07:06,450 --> 00:07:08,160
Anytime!

99
00:07:08,160 --> 00:07:10,910
Maybe the border guards
were just seeing things.

100
00:07:10,910 --> 00:07:12,660
They're leaving.

101
00:07:19,880 --> 00:07:21,750
Sniff, sniff!

102
00:07:20,660 --> 00:07:21,530
Sniff!

103
00:07:27,920 --> 00:07:29,720
Sanji-chan!

104
00:07:29,720 --> 00:07:32,510
That was too much blood! He's in danger!

105
00:07:32,510 --> 00:07:36,390
He couldn't hold it! All that
pent-up excitement exploded!

106
00:07:36,390 --> 00:07:38,270
Sanji!

107
00:07:38,980 --> 00:07:40,690
That's...

108
00:07:40,690 --> 00:07:42,190
No mistaking him.

109
00:07:42,190 --> 00:07:44,560
The pirate - Straw Hat Luffy!

110
00:07:46,910 --> 00:07:49,280
--Ammo Knights!
--Yes, sir!

111
00:08:03,920 --> 00:08:06,760
There they are! Straw Hat and the others.

112
00:08:06,760 --> 00:08:09,340
What should we do? They'll catch them first.

113
00:08:09,340 --> 00:08:13,680
But we don't wanna cause any
trouble with Neptune's army.

114
00:08:17,100 --> 00:08:18,520
Wait a minute!

115
00:08:18,520 --> 00:08:22,860
We're sorry about the illegal entry!
But you can't arrest us now!

116
00:08:22,860 --> 00:08:26,150
Can somebody donate blood now?!

117
00:08:26,150 --> 00:08:30,610
If nothing is done,
our friend is gonna die within an hour!

118
00:08:31,010 --> 00:08:34,320
His blood type is S RH negative.

119
00:08:34,320 --> 00:08:37,110
It's rare but does anybody here share the same blood type?

120
00:08:37,110 --> 00:08:40,370
Or are Fish-Men and Mermaids'
blood totally different?

121
00:08:41,330 --> 00:08:42,580
Chopper-chin.

122
00:08:42,580 --> 00:08:45,380
We don't have time! Anyone?!

123
00:08:45,380 --> 00:08:48,090
This is... This is the dumbest way to die!

124
00:08:48,880 --> 00:08:51,630
Somebody please! I beg you!

125
00:08:51,630 --> 00:08:54,100
Give blood to Sanji!

126
00:08:54,100 --> 00:08:56,720
Luffy-chin, Chopper-chin!

127
00:08:56,940 --> 00:08:58,280
Mermaids and Fish-Men blood

128
00:08:58,280 --> 00:09:01,350
are the same as humans so we can donate blood!

129
00:09:01,630 --> 00:09:02,520
But...

130
00:09:08,480 --> 00:09:12,860
Those humans are talking nonsense!

131
00:09:13,660 --> 00:09:15,620
Those guys with sea monsters!

132
00:09:16,080 --> 00:09:18,910
Prince Fukaboshi, that's Hammond
from the Fish-Man District.

133
00:09:22,290 --> 00:09:25,980
There is nobody on this island who would

134
00:09:25,980 --> 00:09:30,470
give blood to such lowly creatures as humans.

135
00:09:30,890 --> 00:09:32,690
If somebody does,

136
00:09:33,250 --> 00:09:37,600
he risks the Punishment of the Dark Night from human haters.

137
00:09:37,600 --> 00:09:39,100
Punishment?

138
00:09:39,100 --> 00:09:44,560
He can just keep losing
blood helplessly and die!

139
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:48,730
There is this old law in our kingdom.

140
00:09:49,190 --> 00:09:53,280
Donating blood to humans is prohibited.

141
00:09:54,200 --> 00:09:54,780
What?!

142
00:09:54,780 --> 00:10:00,330
Make no mistake!
You humans set the rule first!

143
00:10:00,330 --> 00:10:04,920
You people have a long history
of fearing us as monsters

144
00:10:04,920 --> 00:10:08,540
and refused to get your blood mixed-up!

145
00:10:08,540 --> 00:10:12,800
That's why Fisher Tiger,
the hero of the Fish-Man Island, died.

146
00:10:14,760 --> 00:10:17,140
Fisher... Tiger?

147
00:10:17,140 --> 00:10:21,350
He risked his own life to
free slaves of all races

148
00:10:21,350 --> 00:10:23,270
but after a bloody war,

149
00:10:23,270 --> 00:10:27,900
he lost his life although he could've
survived if he had a transfusion!

150
00:10:28,980 --> 00:10:33,190
Those heartless humans
refused to give blood so he died!

151
00:10:35,150 --> 00:10:38,280
Straw Hat, here is what I want you to do.

152
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:42,050
Just give up on your crewmember's life

153
00:10:42,050 --> 00:10:45,240
and come to the Fish-Man District with us!

154
00:10:45,580 --> 00:10:47,750
The captain of the New Fish-Man Pirates

155
00:10:48,080 --> 00:10:52,050
- Hordy Jones is expecting you guys.

156
00:10:52,420 --> 00:10:54,090
Shut up!

157
00:10:54,090 --> 00:10:57,260
Hey, I don't know about the law but please!

158
00:10:57,260 --> 00:11:00,680
Isn't there anyone with S RH negative?!

159
00:11:01,220 --> 00:11:02,970
I'll do anything to repay you!

160
00:11:02,970 --> 00:11:05,940
Just as long as you save his life now!

161
00:11:06,520 --> 00:11:09,770
I said "It's no use"!

162
00:11:10,730 --> 00:11:11,650
Camie!

163
00:11:11,650 --> 00:11:12,820
If you don't comply...

164
00:11:13,360 --> 00:11:14,780
Second Gear!

165
00:11:17,360 --> 00:11:19,740
...I'll take you by force!

166
00:11:20,450 --> 00:11:21,910
Trawl Net!

167
00:11:22,790 --> 00:11:27,500
I told you that we weren't gonna join you!

168
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:29,000
...Jet...

169
00:11:30,170 --> 00:11:31,500
Pistol!

170
00:11:39,390 --> 00:11:41,760
Luffy, a monster behind you!

171
00:11:50,150 --> 00:11:52,770
Hammond and the others got...

172
00:11:52,770 --> 00:11:57,150
The monster gave up without fighting!

173
00:11:57,150 --> 00:11:58,410
Cool!

174
00:11:58,410 --> 00:12:00,740
What was it? Luffy-chan's unbelievable!

175
00:12:02,080 --> 00:12:03,330
Impressive.

176
00:12:03,870 --> 00:12:05,910
Luffy-chin and everybody!

177
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:14,590
Bring Sanji-chin, too! Let's go to the town!

178
00:12:12,980 --> 00:12:14,560
It's the Ryugu!

179
00:12:15,140 --> 00:12:19,020
There are many humans at the
harbor of the town! Hurry up!

180
00:12:19,020 --> 00:12:20,650
Okay!

181
00:12:31,700 --> 00:12:34,370
Alright, we're ready! Camie, let's go!

182
00:12:34,370 --> 00:12:37,790
Uh-huh! Please, Ryugu-chin,
take us to the town!

183
00:12:37,790 --> 00:12:39,250
Mosu!

184
00:12:39,250 --> 00:12:42,380
Hey you, wait! The Ryugu is Princes'...

185
00:12:42,380 --> 00:12:46,510
I'm sorry! I'll bring it back to
you as soon as we save Sanji-chin!

186
00:12:46,510 --> 00:12:48,720
They're leaving!

187
00:12:48,720 --> 00:12:51,930
We don't have a ride home-fa-mi-re-do!

188
00:12:53,020 --> 00:12:54,310
Hmm.

189
00:12:55,890 --> 00:13:00,820
I'm sorry. If my blood type
matched, I wouldn't refuse.

190
00:13:01,360 --> 00:13:03,920
You don't have to apologize.

191
00:13:03,920 --> 00:13:06,780
It all started because of his lecherous feelings.

192
00:13:07,240 --> 00:13:10,450
Look. He's still smiling a little.

193
00:13:10,450 --> 00:13:14,160
...And at the same time, it's nice and bouncy...

194
00:13:14,520 --> 00:13:18,250
Sanji, that's enough!
Don't think about anything!

195
00:13:18,250 --> 00:13:20,960
You're in a delicate state!

196
00:13:22,880 --> 00:13:27,010
You and Hachi were discriminated
against at Sabaody 2 years ago

197
00:13:27,010 --> 00:13:28,800
so I guess it really runs deep.

198
00:13:28,800 --> 00:13:31,850
I can't believe Sanji's dirty
mind caused such a big issue!

199
00:13:31,850 --> 00:13:35,360
Yeah, and even if we get to the town,

200
00:13:35,360 --> 00:13:37,560
I don't know if we can find a donor right away.

201
00:13:37,560 --> 00:13:38,640
What?

202
00:13:38,640 --> 00:13:43,770
We haven't had that many
human visitors for a month.

203
00:13:43,770 --> 00:13:46,400
You guys are our first visitors in a while.

204
00:13:46,400 --> 00:13:49,320
Why? I thought this was the famous scoop.

205
00:13:49,320 --> 00:13:51,820
Yes, it is a famous spot.

206
00:13:52,050 --> 00:13:53,820
We don't know why.

207
00:13:53,820 --> 00:13:56,710
They say maybe somebody
is standing in the voyagers' way.

208
00:13:57,110 --> 00:14:01,830
Somebody powerful is up to something
- that's the talk of the Kingdom.

209
00:14:05,210 --> 00:14:07,920
That was no good, ladies.

210
00:14:07,920 --> 00:14:10,760
Why were you hiding the pirates?

211
00:14:12,220 --> 00:14:14,720
I'm sorry, Prince Fukaboshi.

212
00:14:14,720 --> 00:14:17,350
They were Camie's friends.

213
00:14:17,350 --> 00:14:22,770
And they were good people and we
didn't want them to be arrested.

214
00:14:23,770 --> 00:14:25,820
I hope Sanji-chan will be fine.

215
00:14:25,820 --> 00:14:30,240
You ladies mistook us.
He's a well-known pirate,

216
00:14:30,240 --> 00:14:33,740
he didn't need to go through immigration.

217
00:14:33,740 --> 00:14:35,830
Because we know his identity.

218
00:14:35,830 --> 00:14:41,500
We were looking for them for
another reason-re-mi-fa!

219
00:14:41,500 --> 00:14:43,170
Oh, is it so?

220
00:14:46,630 --> 00:14:51,510
And we were unable to deliver
the message from Jimbei, as well.

221
00:14:58,110 --> 00:15:02,610
That barrel drifted here along
with Camie's friends. What's in it?

222
00:15:02,610 --> 00:15:04,650
Liquor? Treasure?

223
00:15:04,650 --> 00:15:08,870
I don't know. It's very tightly-sealed.

224
00:15:08,870 --> 00:15:12,120
What do you think? Should
we open it secretly?

225
00:15:12,660 --> 00:15:14,870
Is it okay to do that?

226
00:15:16,210 --> 00:15:17,500
I think so.

227
00:15:17,500 --> 00:15:21,210
Oh? You're well-prepared, Ishilly!

228
00:15:21,550 --> 00:15:25,060
THE RYUGU KINGDOM CORAL HILL

229
00:15:25,060 --> 00:15:27,850
MADAM SHARLEY'S HOUSE

230
00:15:28,580 --> 00:15:30,670
Sanji! Are you awake?

231
00:15:30,670 --> 00:15:31,420
Sanji-chin!

232
00:15:33,630 --> 00:15:35,340
Where am I?

233
00:15:37,460 --> 00:15:38,340
What a relief!

234
00:15:38,340 --> 00:15:40,590
We're in a town at the harbor.

235
00:15:40,590 --> 00:15:44,010
Sanji-chin, you lost almost
all the blood from your body.

236
00:15:45,060 --> 00:15:50,190
I'm so glad that we found the blood donor!

237
00:15:50,190 --> 00:15:51,730
Oh, blood...

238
00:15:54,690 --> 00:15:56,780
What's wrong with me?

239
00:15:56,780 --> 00:16:00,610
Don't get up so fast! You need to rest more.

240
00:16:00,610 --> 00:16:04,530
But why won't the Fish-Men donate blood?

241
00:16:04,530 --> 00:16:09,370
We looked everywhere in the
town but we couldn't find a human.

242
00:16:09,370 --> 00:16:11,960
I almost gave up!

243
00:16:11,960 --> 00:16:15,670
Guys, thank you for doing that.

244
00:16:15,670 --> 00:16:18,760
But I don't remember anything.

245
00:16:18,760 --> 00:16:24,300
Where was I and what was I doing?
I can barely remember...

246
00:16:24,300 --> 00:16:27,180
No, don't think back!

247
00:16:27,180 --> 00:16:30,430
We don't want you to have a nosebleed again!

248
00:16:30,430 --> 00:16:32,490
Oh yeah, Sanji! Let me introduce you

249
00:16:32,490 --> 00:16:36,570
to the blood donor that
we finally found at a bar!

250
00:16:36,770 --> 00:16:38,480
You have to say "thank you"!

251
00:16:39,300 --> 00:16:42,850
Huh? Don't tell me that I got
blood from such a delicate lady!

252
00:16:43,280 --> 00:16:46,940
It's okay! We're both humans.

253
00:16:46,830 --> 00:16:50,410
We have to help each other
when we're in trouble.

254
00:16:51,260 --> 00:16:53,640
It's okay, silly!

255
00:16:53,640 --> 00:16:54,800
If you want...

256
00:16:54,800 --> 00:16:57,520
...We can give you more, silly!

257
00:17:05,530 --> 00:17:07,490
I'm glad that he's back to his old self!

258
00:17:09,330 --> 00:17:11,870
Hey, say "thank you" to them!

259
00:17:12,700 --> 00:17:16,210
Luffy, let me see your right arm.

260
00:17:21,460 --> 00:17:23,340
Positive reaction for poison!

261
00:17:23,340 --> 00:17:26,470
That's a poisonous wound as I thought!

262
00:17:26,470 --> 00:17:30,140
Come to think of it, when I
fought against the Fish-Men...

263
00:17:31,100 --> 00:17:32,560
I felt something sting me.

264
00:17:33,600 --> 00:17:36,650
But you're okay?

265
00:17:36,650 --> 00:17:37,440
Uh-huh.

266
00:17:37,440 --> 00:17:39,110
Okay, let me see it.

267
00:17:40,110 --> 00:17:43,320
This must be deadly poison.
Are you really okay?

268
00:17:43,320 --> 00:17:43,820
Uh-huh.

269
00:17:43,820 --> 00:17:45,950
I can't believe it!

270
00:17:45,950 --> 00:17:51,660
An antibody must have developed
in your body to counter such poison.

271
00:17:51,660 --> 00:17:55,620
Have you ever been poisoned before?

272
00:17:55,620 --> 00:17:57,080
Poison, huh?

273
00:18:00,710 --> 00:18:04,730
I almost died from
poisoning in the Impel Down.

274
00:18:07,630 --> 00:18:10,930
Almost died? It's not funny!

275
00:18:10,930 --> 00:18:12,800
I think it was that guy!

276
00:18:13,190 --> 00:18:15,410
The swordsman with octopus tentacles.

277
00:18:15,770 --> 00:18:18,930
He blocked my punch!

278
00:18:19,350 --> 00:18:21,420
I bet he's very strong!

279
00:18:30,690 --> 00:18:32,440
That's coming from the cove.

280
00:18:32,910 --> 00:18:35,900
Those Mermaids are really noisy.

281
00:18:36,370 --> 00:18:38,870
Now what should I do?

282
00:18:38,870 --> 00:18:41,630
These guys are all messed-up.

283
00:18:42,090 --> 00:18:46,550
And I accidentally poisoned Straw Hat.

284
00:18:46,550 --> 00:18:48,630
I'll be in trouble if he dies.

285
00:18:49,970 --> 00:18:52,760
Ishilly and the others were screaming!

286
00:18:52,760 --> 00:18:56,770
Ishilly!

287
00:18:56,770 --> 00:18:58,980
I heard them around here!

288
00:18:58,980 --> 00:19:00,900
Where did they go?

289
00:19:00,900 --> 00:19:04,360
I heard them talking about opening a barrel.

290
00:19:05,920 --> 00:19:10,040
Everyone, come here.
There's somebody I'd like you to meet.

291
00:19:13,920 --> 00:19:16,560
The owner of the Mermaid
Cafe who let Sanji stay...

292
00:19:16,560 --> 00:19:18,030
What is this?

293
00:19:18,030 --> 00:19:19,720
...Madam Sharley.

294
00:19:19,720 --> 00:19:20,970
Oh yeah? Thanks!

295
00:19:23,020 --> 00:19:25,770
Is the blond boy okay now?

296
00:19:24,890 --> 00:19:28,650
THE OWNER OF THE MERMAID CAFE MADAM SHARLEY

297
00:19:25,770 --> 00:19:28,650
Uh-huh. But since you're
such a beautiful lady,

298
00:19:29,010 --> 00:19:31,610
it's best you stay away from the room.

299
00:19:31,610 --> 00:19:35,460
And let's not tell Sanji-chin
that this place is in the

300
00:19:35,960 --> 00:19:37,540
back of the Mermaid Cafe.

301
00:19:37,830 --> 00:19:39,090
Why's that?

302
00:19:39,320 --> 00:19:44,910
His doctor, Chopper-chin said that if
he finds out, there'll be trouble again.

303
00:19:44,910 --> 00:19:47,670
What a strange prognosis.

304
00:19:48,290 --> 00:19:50,790
Hey, Big Mermaid!

305
00:19:50,790 --> 00:19:53,420
It's Madam Sharley, Luffy-chin!

306
00:19:53,820 --> 00:19:56,090
--What's this?
--It's beautiful!

307
00:19:56,090 --> 00:19:59,420
Don't touch it, Straw Hat boys.

308
00:20:00,090 --> 00:20:03,260
That's the crystal ball she
uses to look into the future.

309
00:20:03,640 --> 00:20:07,750
Madam's pre-vision is
famous in the Coral Hill.

310
00:20:08,900 --> 00:20:11,730
I'm not practicing anymore.

311
00:20:16,610 --> 00:20:20,030
It's better not knowing the future.

312
00:20:21,280 --> 00:20:24,360
Well, how about this? Do you Mermaids poop?

313
00:20:25,170 --> 00:20:27,540
What does that have to
do with her pre-vision?

314
00:20:27,540 --> 00:20:28,710
Don't you have any class?

315
00:20:29,870 --> 00:20:31,920
A-Apologize to her, Luffy-chin!

316
00:20:32,430 --> 00:20:33,420
Sorry.

317
00:20:34,070 --> 00:20:38,470
Camie, you can take a day off today.

318
00:20:38,470 --> 00:20:40,720
Show them around the island.

319
00:20:41,120 --> 00:20:42,470
Huh? Really?

320
00:20:42,470 --> 00:20:45,280
You always work hard.

321
00:20:45,620 --> 00:20:46,390
And...

322
00:20:47,100 --> 00:20:50,950
...these days we don't
have human pirate guests

323
00:20:50,950 --> 00:20:52,990
and my business is drying up.

324
00:20:53,730 --> 00:20:55,930
The girls from the cove will come soon

325
00:20:55,930 --> 00:20:58,030
so we have enough hands (hitode).

326
00:20:58,030 --> 00:21:00,280
Enough starfish (hitode)...

327
00:21:00,280 --> 00:21:04,830
Oh no! I should have delivered
those clams to Pappagu by now!

328
00:21:05,700 --> 00:21:07,830
That was so out-of-context!

329
00:21:07,830 --> 00:21:10,580
He must be hungry...

330
00:21:10,530 --> 00:21:17,540
What? Monsieur Pappagu is having
fun at the cafe with his old friend.

331
00:21:17,540 --> 00:21:18,790
At the cafe?

332
00:21:18,790 --> 00:21:21,210
Old friend?

333
00:21:26,920 --> 00:21:29,070
I couldn't mention this in front of her,

334
00:21:29,650 --> 00:21:31,990
but when Madam was a little child,

335
00:21:32,800 --> 00:21:36,100
she said that many pirates
would come to the island.

336
00:21:36,600 --> 00:21:41,140
That was the year before
the Great Pirate Era began.

337
00:21:41,140 --> 00:21:42,630
What?!

338
00:21:43,460 --> 00:21:45,590
Among a host of other things,

339
00:21:45,590 --> 00:21:48,220
she recently predicted the war at Marineford

340
00:21:48,220 --> 00:21:50,650
and Whitebeard's death.

341
00:21:50,650 --> 00:21:52,010
What?!

342
00:21:52,650 --> 00:21:56,070
She can't stand knowing
what bad things will happen.

343
00:21:56,070 --> 00:21:57,780
Must be scary!

344
00:21:57,780 --> 00:21:59,120
Where's Chopper?

345
00:21:59,120 --> 00:22:02,040
Oh, he's taking care of Sanji.

346
00:22:02,040 --> 00:22:04,820
--Luffy-chin! Usopp-chin!
--Yeah!

347
00:22:07,970 --> 00:22:11,010
This is the main street of Coral Hill.

348
00:22:11,010 --> 00:22:14,630
Look! That's the entrance
of the Mermaid Cafe.

349
00:22:18,230 --> 00:22:20,810
Oh, I'm getting hungry!

350
00:22:20,810 --> 00:22:22,390
It's a cafe!

351
00:22:22,390 --> 00:22:25,940
We have food too! Cakes and sea fruit.

352
00:22:25,940 --> 00:22:27,520
What about meat?

353
00:22:27,520 --> 00:22:31,320
We Merfolk don't eat meat and fish

354
00:22:31,320 --> 00:22:35,200
so what we have is; Wakame Brûlée,
Mozuku Tart, Kelp Soufflé...

355
00:22:35,200 --> 00:22:37,450
Are they edible?

356
00:22:37,450 --> 00:22:40,330
--Oh, we have meat too!
--What?

357
00:22:40,330 --> 00:22:44,210
Shellfish meat! Scallop
Sandwich, Freshwater Clam Pizza...

358
00:22:44,210 --> 00:22:47,130
That's not meat!
Don't ruin meat's reputation!

359
00:22:47,130 --> 00:22:50,460
Whoa... Anyway, let's
go in! The Mermaid Cafe!

360
00:22:50,460 --> 00:22:52,880
Yeah, Pappagu will be there.

361
00:22:52,880 --> 00:22:55,130
Hey, don't ruin meat's reputation!

362
00:22:55,130 --> 00:22:58,140
Thank you very much!

363
00:22:59,720 --> 00:23:01,810
Resting my bones! Resting my bones!

364
00:23:02,470 --> 00:23:04,480
I'm happy for you, Bone!

365
00:23:04,170 --> 00:23:06,840
--Brook!
--Brook-chin!

366
00:23:06,840 --> 00:23:12,560
Oh, Luffy-san and Usopp-san!
And it's been a while, Camie-san!

367
00:23:11,300 --> 00:23:12,630
She's a Mermaid!

368
00:23:12,630 --> 00:23:14,470
Straw! Nose!

369
00:23:14,930 --> 00:23:19,390
I missed you guys!
I didn't know that you were here!

370
00:23:19,390 --> 00:23:20,890
Long time no see!

371
00:23:20,890 --> 00:23:23,560
So you were with Pappagu!

372
00:23:23,520 --> 00:23:25,810
Soul King, come to see us again!

373
00:23:23,560 --> 00:23:28,480
Yes, I didn't expect to be
rescued by Pappagu-san!

374
00:23:26,810 --> 00:23:29,150
I had a wonderful time!

375
00:23:30,810 --> 00:23:34,520
I'll be back, beautiful Mermaids!

376
00:23:34,520 --> 00:23:35,650
What?!

377
00:23:36,190 --> 00:23:37,650
I'm going boneless!

378
00:23:39,360 --> 00:23:43,070
Oh, I can't exist without bones!

379
00:23:43,070 --> 00:23:45,660
Oh, I don't care if I die now!

380
00:23:45,660 --> 00:23:48,290
Oh no, I'm already dead!

381
00:23:48,290 --> 00:23:49,580
How cool!

382
00:23:49,580 --> 00:23:52,580
He got so hyper in the cafe...

383
00:23:52,580 --> 00:23:54,880
Yeah, I wonder what's going on inside.

384
00:23:54,880 --> 00:23:56,630
Wait, wait, wait!

385
00:23:57,710 --> 00:24:00,010
You aren't leaving today, are you?

386
00:24:00,010 --> 00:24:02,130
I know you are interested in the cafe

387
00:24:02,130 --> 00:24:05,460
but you can come back with everybody later.

388
00:24:05,810 --> 00:24:10,640
I was gonna take Bone to my house now.

389
00:24:12,270 --> 00:24:15,020
Come with me! Do you like sea monster meat?

390
00:24:15,020 --> 00:24:16,880
Do you have meat?!

391
00:24:18,900 --> 00:24:23,200
I'm wild, I don't wanna eat
seaweed or shellfish!

392
00:24:23,200 --> 00:24:26,490
What I mainly eat is violent sea monsters!

393
00:24:27,070 --> 00:24:30,200
Oh, Pappagu, I almost forget!
Here are your clams for today.

394
00:24:30,200 --> 00:24:33,260
Yeah! Camie's best clams!

395
00:24:33,670 --> 00:24:35,210
So you eat shellfish!

396
00:24:35,210 --> 00:24:36,670
Damn!

397
00:24:37,180 --> 00:24:41,480
Unlike Merfolk, Fish-Men eat meat and fish.

398
00:24:41,480 --> 00:24:44,600
It's not like we don't have them here.

399
00:24:44,600 --> 00:24:46,690
Oh, glad to hear that!

400
00:24:46,690 --> 00:24:49,610
Oh, just what I was looking for! Hey, taxi!

401
00:24:49,610 --> 00:24:51,900
Here I go!

402
00:24:53,110 --> 00:24:54,780
What?!

403
00:24:57,070 --> 00:25:01,700
Vander Decken! He's a ghost -
Why are they looking for him?!

404
00:25:01,700 --> 00:25:04,920
Oh, this guy was on the
ghost ship that we saw?

405
00:25:05,500 --> 00:25:08,130
--What?! Did you guys see him?
--Yes.

406
00:25:08,590 --> 00:25:12,410
The whole nation has been
looking for him for years!

407
00:25:12,410 --> 00:25:15,200
He's a pirate--an undersea bandit!

408
00:25:15,510 --> 00:25:18,800
I'll tell you about it later. Get on first!

409
00:25:23,590 --> 00:25:27,680
Vander Decken was sending love letters...

410
00:25:27,680 --> 00:25:32,430
...to the Mermaid Princess of the
Ryugu Kingdom at least once a week.

411
00:25:33,600 --> 00:25:38,690
Before long, the letters became
packages, then threats to marry him...

412
00:25:38,690 --> 00:25:41,280
Oh, it's fluffy! Feels good!

413
00:25:41,280 --> 00:25:44,490
Yeah, it's like heaven!

414
00:25:44,490 --> 00:25:46,610
Listen to a starfish!

415
00:25:46,610 --> 00:25:48,660
--Okay!
--Oh, sorry.

416
00:25:49,830 --> 00:25:54,120
His eccentric behavior made
the Mermaid Princess afraid

417
00:25:54,120 --> 00:25:57,920
and it became a national concern...

418
00:25:57,920 --> 00:26:02,050
Yeah, the Mermaid Princess'
father - King Neptune got mad

419
00:26:02,510 --> 00:26:04,680
and those 3 princes that we just met

420
00:26:04,680 --> 00:26:07,680
have been looking for him with the army

421
00:26:07,680 --> 00:26:09,320
but they can't find him.

422
00:26:09,640 --> 00:26:13,520
Camie, Camie... I was just
telling them about it...

423
00:26:13,520 --> 00:26:17,810
King Neptune, the God of the Sea,
who runs this country...

424
00:26:17,810 --> 00:26:21,940
...has 4 children including
the Mermaid Princess.

425
00:26:21,940 --> 00:26:27,910
The Mermaid Princess is the youngest
and the 3 princes are older than her.

426
00:26:27,910 --> 00:26:30,070
Hey, Camie...

427
00:26:30,070 --> 00:26:33,240
But what I can't understand is

428
00:26:33,240 --> 00:26:40,250
Vander Deck must be a ghostly
pirate from hundreds of years ago...

429
00:26:40,960 --> 00:26:45,590
Well, those legends are often exaggerated.

430
00:26:46,130 --> 00:26:48,250
He truly existed and in fact,

431
00:26:48,250 --> 00:26:51,940
I heard that the legendary
captain--Vander Decken...

432
00:26:51,940 --> 00:26:56,650
...reached the Fish-Man Island and died here.

433
00:26:57,060 --> 00:27:02,730
The ship that you saw was the
Flying Dutchman, wasn't it?

434
00:27:03,570 --> 00:27:06,190
It's his descendent who is on the ship!

435
00:27:07,780 --> 00:27:10,160
Vander Decken IX!

436
00:27:12,700 --> 00:27:14,580
What?! His descendent?!

437
00:27:14,580 --> 00:27:16,560
Oh, is that so?

438
00:27:16,560 --> 00:27:18,650
That means he's not a ghost.

439
00:27:18,650 --> 00:27:20,740
I thought that it was a real ghost and felt

440
00:27:20,740 --> 00:27:23,390
more dead than alive since I'm a skeleton.

441
00:27:23,390 --> 00:27:26,800
That's good. That's just good.

442
00:27:26,800 --> 00:27:29,550
Camie... Camie... Camie...

443
00:27:30,840 --> 00:27:35,390
When I look closer,
Merfolk and Fish-Men are all different.

444
00:27:35,390 --> 00:27:39,350
There are old Mermaids! Like Grandma Kokoro!

445
00:27:39,350 --> 00:27:41,350
Look, there's a baby!

446
00:27:42,360 --> 00:27:46,400
The father is a Fish-Man and the
children are Merfolk and Fish-Men.

447
00:27:46,770 --> 00:27:49,740
When a Mermaid and a Fish-Man get married,

448
00:27:49,740 --> 00:27:54,490
their kids would be either Merfolk
or Fish-Man, either boy or girl.

449
00:27:51,780 --> 00:27:54,700
So there are 4 possibilities.

450
00:27:54,700 --> 00:27:57,440
Hmmm, that's why they're all different.

451
00:27:57,440 --> 00:27:58,830
Interesting!

452
00:27:59,170 --> 00:28:01,130
Alright, let's get on the highway!

453
00:28:06,220 --> 00:28:07,470
It's fast!

454
00:28:08,460 --> 00:28:09,900
What's that?

455
00:28:09,900 --> 00:28:12,180
That's a candy factory.

456
00:28:12,180 --> 00:28:15,060
No, why is there a pirate flag?!

457
00:28:15,060 --> 00:28:17,640
That? You can see the same flag at the

458
00:28:17,640 --> 00:28:20,240
entrance of the island and at the harbor.

459
00:28:20,240 --> 00:28:23,820
That flag is protecting
the Fish-Man Island.

460
00:28:24,280 --> 00:28:29,030
The mark belongs to a pirate called
Charlotte Linlin of the New World.

461
00:28:29,030 --> 00:28:32,740
Also known as Big Mam,
one of The Four Emperors!

462
00:28:32,740 --> 00:28:34,580
Th-The Four Emperors?

463
00:28:35,700 --> 00:28:41,880
Before the war, Whitebeard was
protecting the island from pirates

464
00:28:41,880 --> 00:28:44,130
but now it's Big Mam.

465
00:28:44,130 --> 00:28:46,010
Hmmm.

466
00:28:46,010 --> 00:28:50,720
But she demands a lot of sweet
candies every month in exchange.

467
00:28:50,720 --> 00:28:53,180
That's what the factory is for.

468
00:28:53,180 --> 00:28:54,140
Candies?

469
00:28:54,610 --> 00:28:59,690
This country can't exist without the
protection of those powerful people.

470
00:28:59,690 --> 00:29:04,070
That's how dangerous this place is,
where pirates come and go frequently.

471
00:29:04,070 --> 00:29:07,790
But she's protecting the country
after old man Whitebeard.

472
00:29:07,790 --> 00:29:09,610
Isn't Big Mam a good person?

473
00:29:10,070 --> 00:29:11,310
It's hard to say.

474
00:29:11,310 --> 00:29:14,400
Whitebeard never demanded anything.

475
00:29:14,700 --> 00:29:18,250
So Big Mam views it as business, maybe.

476
00:29:18,250 --> 00:29:20,160
Big Mam...

477
00:29:20,160 --> 00:29:22,170
One of The Four Emperors like Shanks.

478
00:29:22,490 --> 00:29:24,250
Wonder if I'll meet her someday.

479
00:29:24,660 --> 00:29:26,230
Look forward!

480
00:29:26,500 --> 00:29:30,170
We're in Fishverly Hills,
the town of the celebs!

481
00:29:31,590 --> 00:29:35,640
That tall building right in
front of us is Pappagu's house.

482
00:29:35,640 --> 00:29:38,600
That?! That's too much for a starfish!

483
00:29:44,940 --> 00:29:46,840
We have to do something!

484
00:29:48,580 --> 00:29:51,300
She's a madam from the Mermaid Cafe.

485
00:29:51,650 --> 00:29:55,780
What's the matter, Madam Sharley?
Why are you so upset?

486
00:29:56,080 --> 00:29:59,080
We have to do something before it's too late!

487
00:29:59,400 --> 00:30:01,500
Hey, Madam! What's wrong?

488
00:30:03,750 --> 00:30:05,210
Look for him!

489
00:30:05,700 --> 00:30:08,630
The pirate boy with a straw hat!

490
00:30:10,350 --> 00:30:13,720
And throw him out of this country!

491
00:30:13,720 --> 00:30:15,930
Is it a pre-vision again?

492
00:30:15,930 --> 00:30:18,200
I wasn't planning on using it.

493
00:30:18,200 --> 00:30:20,770
But I felt something about him

494
00:30:20,770 --> 00:30:23,490
so I couldn't help looking into the future!

495
00:30:26,380 --> 00:30:29,440
What's wrong?! What did you see?!

496
00:30:29,440 --> 00:30:30,900
Madam!

497
00:30:31,230 --> 00:30:33,070
Sharley! Say it!

498
00:30:33,350 --> 00:30:35,280
--Madam!
--Madam!

499
00:30:36,370 --> 00:30:39,700
I hope it won't happen!
I hope it'll be proven wrong!

500
00:30:46,130 --> 00:30:49,070
A human with a straw hat on...

501
00:30:51,300 --> 00:30:55,810
At Straw Hat Luffy's
hands...  at his hands...

502
00:30:55,810 --> 00:30:57,350
the Fish-Man Island will be...

503
00:30:59,730 --> 00:31:01,360
...destroyed!!
